Whisper: an update address for the update test, on this computer only

What: if the pref whisper.update.testURL holds an http address on 127.0.0.1 or
[::1] (with a port), the update service checks there instead of Whisper's update host.
Any other value is ignored.
Why: the end-to-end update test (gecko/scripts/update/) serves update.xml and MARs
from a local server inside a network namespace and points a test profile at it. The
pref cannot send update checks to another computer, and an update found there must
still pass the same signature, channel and version checks.
---
diff --git a/toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs b/toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs
index d1eeb75f30..8709999222 100644
--- a/toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/mozapps/update/UpdateService.sys.mjs
@@ -5505,6 +5505,16 @@ export class CheckerService {
     let url = Services.appinfo.updateURL;
     let updatePin;
 
+    // Whisper: the update test (gecko/scripts/update/) serves updates from this
+    // computer. Only an http address on the loopback interface is accepted, so
+    // this pref cannot send update checks anywhere else, and every update still
+    // has to carry Whisper's signature.
+    let testURL = Services.prefs.getStringPref("whisper.update.testURL", "");
+    if (/^http:\/\/(127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\]):\d+\//.test(testURL)) {
+      LOG("CheckerService:getUpdateURL - using whisper.update.testURL");
+      url = testURL;
+    }
+
     if (Services.policies) {
       let policies = Services.policies.getActivePolicies();
       if (policies) {
